{"diagnosis": "mem_la_addr low bits are 2'b10 instead of 2'b00, so every lookahead fetch/data address is misaligned by 2. Trace reports TRAP: fetch misalign addr low bits nonzero with tohost FAIL 0xdead. Root cause is line 382 hardcoding {..,2'b10} in both branches of mem_la_addr.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -382 +382 @@
-	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b10} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b10};
+	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b00} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b00};", "expected": "tohost PASS, no TRAP fetch misalign, fetch alignment clean"}

